      "tag": "Standard English",
      "h2": "Shared core",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Standard English</strong> is the form used in news, exams and most writing. It's not 'correct' speech — just shared.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Accent vs dialect",
      "h2": "Sound vs words",
      "body_html": "<p>An <strong>accent</strong> is how words sound. A <strong>dialect</strong> is the words and grammar themselves ('I were' instead of 'I was').</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Slang & colloquial",
      "h2": "Casual speech",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Slang</strong> is informal and often new ('peng', 'banger'). <strong>Colloquial</strong> covers everyday phrasing. Both are valid in casual contexts.</p>"
    }
